knut@bbri.harvard.edu wrote:

> hi,
>
> we just got a dec personal workstation 500au runniung unix.  we are
> in the process of setting it up, and have a couple questions.
>
> 1.  how do we set it up to recognize another machine on our network
> that is our domain name server?  our internet configuration is set up,
> and works if you put in the ip addresses.  i couldn't see where to
> put in the ip address for the domain name server.

From the System Management Checklist app that should be showing when you log
in as "root",
run the "BIND Setup" application.

>
>
> 2.  how do we enable user login, both at the console and via telnet
> clients.  at present, only root can login at the console.  all others,
> including users at the console, get the message "too many users", even
> if no one else is logged in.

Make sure you've installed your licenses on the pieces of paper that came
with the machine. Use the License
Administration Utility also on the Checklist app. Unless you've purchased
additional licenses, the OSF-BASE license only allows 2 users to be logged
in simultaneously (I don't think "root" is included in that count).

-Jeff D.


