In article <34A1DFB8.CAD9FE44@fallingrain.com>, carl@fallingrain.com wrote:

> Hi All,
> 
>       Just had a couple of the new RZ1DB 9.1Gb drives installed into
> a 2100A running Digital Unix 4.0.
> 
>      To use them seems to require the appropriate entry for /etc/disktab,
> cylinder information etc. The RZ1DB is a new drive, and doesn't have
> an entry in our /etc/disktab.
> 
>      I havn't been able to find this information anywhere on the Digital
web site.
> 
>     Where can I get this entry? Is there a way to bring the disk online
without
> it?

    When in doubt, try 'man disklabel' --- it worked for our RZ40-AA (the
narrow version of the 9.1 Gbyte drive):

type: SCSI
disk: RZ40-AA
label:
flags: dynamic_geometry
bytes/sector: 512
sectors/track: 152
tracks/cylinder: 20
sectors/cylinder: 3040
cylinders: 5273
sectors/unit: 17773524
rpm: 7200
interleave: 1
trackskew: 9
cylinderskew: 9
headswitch: 0           # milliseconds
track-to-track seek: 0  # milliseconds
drivedata: 0

    Thenice thing about Digital UNIX is that you can just use disklabel
and forget about /etc/disktab.

    Hope this helps,

                  Joe Gurman

