Mats Bergstrom wrote:

> Hello,
>   Maybe this is well known, but I have not been able to find any references...
>
> DECthreads bugcheck (version V3.13-435), terminating execution.
> vpUpcallThreadUnblocked: (os/kern) invalid argument (4) nxm_resched(13,0)

Known bug (QAR 51214). It's a fairly subtle race condition between the user mode
scheduler and a kernel thread, and it's been fixed since the "bl5" consolidated patch
kits for 4.0, 4.0A, and 4.0B. (You don't say which you're using.)

Check in ftp://ftp.service.digital.com/public/Digital_UNIX/ under the appropriate
branch (v4.0, v4.0a, v4.0b, or v4.0c). Note that the public areas seem to have really
old patch kits for 4.0 and 4.0a (bl4), and those don't have the proper fix. The latest
listed for 4.0b (though still old) does have it. If you have a service contract, you
might possibly find more recent kits under the "Contract ACCESS" button on the
http://www.service.digital.com/html/patch_main.html page (though I can't verify that).

