Let's see...100K users, 2K document, 30 seconds. That's a theoretical peak
load of 200MB/30sec,
or 1600Mb/30sec, or 53 Mb/sec. You can get that down an OC3 pipe, but
where's it all going to
go once it hits your ISP?

Think "server farm". Look into the Cisco Local Director and something like
a bunch of Sun
Ultra 2's behind it. That approach will do wonders for your expected
availability, too.

