Andrew Ireland wrote in message
<882447391.7821.0.nnrp-03.9e982017@news.demon.co.uk>...

>Is there any way to configure syslog to create a log directory which will
>log  files
>and create new directories say once per month?


Thanks to all who replied, here I am answering my own question.

#!/bin/ksh
month=`date +"%b"`
echo "local1.info       /var/adm/syslog/log.$month" >
/etc/syslog.conf.monthly
#
# in /etc we have a copy of the original daily log, called syslog.conf.daily
# cat the daily and the monthly file together to /etc/syslog.conf
#
cat /etc/syslog.conf.daily /etc/syslog.conf.monthly  > /etc/syslog.conf
#
# it doesn't matter if we overwrite the old syslog.conf file as the syslogd
# will have a note of all the file descriptors
#

If this is run in the root cron script at the beginning of the month
_before_ the
daily restart then when the syslog restarts  on the new month it will create
the new files.





