X-Deja-AN: 308596206
References: <34997739.3B217293@alpha.delta.edu>
X-MimeOLE: Produced By Microsoft MimeOLE V4.71.1712.3
Organization: Bucknell University
Newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1


John F. Plachta wrote in message <34997739.3B217293@alpha.delta.edu>...
>currently running 3.2d-1.  Any ideas would be appreciated.


Run netstat and see how many sockets are in FIN_WAIT_2 state.  We've noticed
a lot of sockets "stuck" in that state (especially on web server sockets),
and apparently this eventually drains the system of resources needed to
service other ports (like telnetd).

For more information on the FIN_WAIT_2 problem, look at
<http://www.apache.org/docs/misc/fin_wait_2.html>, in the context of the
Apache web server, but the problem spills over into other services.  Wish I
had a reasonable fix for this (other than moving our web server off a
multi-user machine!)





