> T3/OC3 (If you have any suggestions on connection "pipes", I would
> appreciate them as well.)

If the sum total of the pages that the users might download is only a
few gigabytes, and no cgi scripts are involved, you have a trivially
parallel situation and you could just buy a bunch of low end
workstations -- Ultra 2's, or PentiumII's running Linux -- and have
the web pages reside on local disk on every node. It's cheap and
scalable.

Then you can use rdist or sup or something less buggy to keep
the pages themselves synchronized on all the systems.

-- g




