Hi all,

Can I configure quota to use the NIS database map?

A brief description of our setup follows: we have a central AlphaStation
(Digital UNIX V3.2c) which exports users volumes via automount to a
cluster of Digital UNIX boxes of various flavours. Currently, users check
their quotas via a simple shell script which launches a remote shell on our
server and returns. It works, but is not a neat solution.

Alternatively, I could put the users disks in the /etc/fstab of all the
workstations in our cluster;
-- cut --
# local volumes
/dev/rz0a        /        ufs rw 1 1
/proc            /proc    procfs rw 0 0
/dev/rz0g        /usr     ufs rw 1 2
/dev/rz0b        swap1    ufs sw 0 2
#remote volumes
/u/pol1a/@pol1   /u/pol1a nfs rq,userquota 0 0
/u/pol1b/@pol1   /u/pol1b nfs rq,userquota 0 0
-- cut --
where 'pol1' is the name of our server and 'pol1a' + 'pol1b' are users
volumes. However, this defeats the object of using automount. Plus, could
get difficult to maintain.

