Douglas B. Jones wrote:
> 
> We have a hp laserjet 5si/5s mx with duplex ability. I print to it via
> remote printing. Regardless of which -K option I use in lpr, it is ignored
> by the printer. If the printer is set to two sided, then -K1 has no effect
> and if it is set to one sided then -K2 has no effect. Does anyone have any
> idea how we can set the hp to respect the -K option?
> 
> Thanks in advance.
> Cheers,
> Douglas

When printing via lpd remote it is the responsibility of the remote
system to process all the lpr options. While it wasn't stated I 
suspect the remote system is really the printer network card. If so,
it is the printers responsibility to handle the -K option, which it
can't.

The generic solution is to switch over to tcp/ip socket printing and
use an appropriate print filter.

Step 1:
        You must have v4.0A or later installed to utilize tcp/ip socket
        printing. The setup instructions are in the release notes
        for V4.0A and I believe in the system admin guide for V4.0B
        and later.

Step 2:
        The print filter. Since the 5simx is a postscript printer I
        would try the ln03rof print filter. I can't test the
 	configuration but I believe that this setup will provided 
	the following:

                - text to postscript conversion
                - landscape printing
                - duplex printing.
                - and possible tray selection using lpr -I# where #
                  is a number starting from 0 and probably not 
		  exceeding 5.

        This setup does not handle PCL formatted files. If the file 
	does have PCL commands use lpr -x file.



