Sorry to follow-up on my own post, but I found the solution
and noticed at least one other person that encountered the
problem (without seeing the answer posted here), so here goes:

The problem is the /etc/sysconfigtab file...it is improperly
created for the device.  Specifically, it should read as follows:

wdd_dnses:
        Module_Config_Name = wdd_dnses
        EISA_Option = Board_Id - 'DEC2F00', Function_Name - DNSES,
Driver_Name - wdd_dnses, Type - C, Adpt_Config - N


The change is in the function name section...the original stated
Null, the new version states DNSES.

More details at:

http://www-archive.stanford.edu/lists/alpha-osf-managers/hyper97/5269.html




