X-Deja-AN: 295419131
References: <665vus$31n@antares.utu.fi>
Organization: Crop Protection
Newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1


You'll find the information I think you are looking for in the Digital UNIX
4.0b release notes section 3.3.2 page 3-3.
for X11 it requires editing  /usr/lib/X11/xdm/Xservers and changing
":0 local /usr/bin/X11/X -nice2" to
":0 local /usr/bin/X11/X -nice2 -screen 0 800"

for CDE it requires editing /usr/dt/config/Xservers and Xservers.con
":0 Local local@console /usr/bin/X11/X :0 -nice2" to
":0 Local local@console /usr/bin/X11/X :0 -nice2 -screen0 800"

make sure your screen supports 800x600 before you do this.  
Hope it Works for you.

Mark 


