One other place to check is "/usr/adm/syslog.dated/*/*.log".  These
are text files.  In particular, look at kern.log.

I recommend this because we saw similar "CPU EXCEPTION" errors in
uerf.  Corresponding with each uerf entry was a syslog.dated entry
(in kern.log, if I remember) stating there was a corrected "dcache"
error.  This happened on an AlphaStation 500/500.  After replacing
the CPU/motherboard, the error was still there.  Then 256meg RAM was
then replaced and the errors went away.

