>>>>> "MRB" == Mark R Bowyer <Mark.Bowyer@uk.sun.com> writes:

  MRB> I'm also not sure what makes an XPM usable from one tool, and
  MRB> unusable from another.  Definately the colour count it
  MRB> important.  I used to think it was the number of hex digits in
  MRB> the colour key in the index at the top, but I'm not so sure
  MRB> now.

The key is how many characters the xpm in question uses to represent a 
pixel. CDE can only handle XPM's which use 1 characther = 1 pixel,
whereas programs that use the standard Xpm library can use
multicharacter pixels. I believe that xv will create usable pixmaps
when the color usage is under 38 colors, though it's been a long time
since I tested that out.

-Larry
(Speaking for myself, not HP)

